    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d192">

                <pb facs="0488" n="446" sameAs="frus:frus1951v04p1/pg446"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">No. 192</seg>
                </opener>
                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.5/11–2151: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Acting Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret   priority</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-11-21T17:00:00+01:00">November 21,
                            1951—5 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3049. For Webb from Acheson and Harriman. Referring Deptel 2999,<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d192-f1"/> commitment given French at mtg Pleven on Friday morning
                    (Embtel 2967<anchor n="2" xml:id="d192-f2"/>) was assurance that $600 million
                    (excluding possible $50 million ExIm Bank cotton loan) of expenditures wld be
                    achieved in France before June 30, 1952, through one means or another, provided
                    French did necessary things with respect to bases and other facilities, and on
                    assumption French come up with adequate contribution to defense of West Eur
                    within the overall NATO framework being developed by TCC and continue Indochina
                    effort. No indication given re specific breakdown of figure, but understanding
                    on US side was that it might possibly be $300 million econ aid and $300 million
                    US military expenditures. Our view was that to extent military expenditures shld
                    exceed $300 million, we cld reduce econ aid figure. It was not contemplated by
                    us that econ aid <pb facs="0489" n="447" xml:id="pg447"/> wld exceed $300
                    million. Consequently do not envisage asking for transfer to France under
                    Section 101(b) of more than $180 million and then only on conditions and
                    assumptions set forth above.</p>
                <p>Any action with respect to a possible transfer shld be held in abeyance pending
                    further word from Mr. Harriman, which will follow discussion between him and
                    Secy Def.</p>
                <p>Pls bring this to President’s attention.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d192-f3"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d192-f1" n="1" xml:id="d192-f1-content">
                <p>Telegram 2999 reported that Webb had forwarded telegram 2967 to the President as
                    requested. (740.5/11–2051)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d192-f2" n="2" xml:id="d192-f2-content">
                <p>Document 190.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d192-f3" n="3" xml:id="d192-f3-content">
                <p>This telegram was sent to the President under a covering memorandum, November 28.
                    (740.5/11–2151)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
